{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 05:13:06 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Path Traversal Analysis - read_file.py: CRITICAL FINDING - Path resolution with .resolve() follows symlinks BEFORE policy enforcement. While denylist covers .env, .git/, ~/.ssh, /etc, /proc, /sys - symlink traversal could bypass relative path checks if attacker creates symlink inside repo pointing to sensitive files. The policy check happens on line 1797 AFTER resolve() on line 1734. | area=path_traversal; confidence=0.85; files_examined=[\"tools/read_file.py\"]; finding_type=symlink_bypass_risk; lines_of_interest=[1730, 1734, 1797]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Traced path from input through expanduser(), resolve(), relative_to(), and _enforce_path_policy(). Examined denylist patterns and matching logic.\", \"what\": \"Found .resolve() called before policy check. Denylist exists but uses pattern matching that may not catch all symlink escapes. allow_outside_repo flag can disable repo boundary entirely.\", \"why\": \"Path traversal is critical - must verify boundary enforcement handles symlinks and ../ sequences\"}; severity=HIGH; stage=research; task=security_audit; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:13:06.839047+00:00_26dd409f", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:13:06.839084+00:00"}
