{"op": "append", "content": "[\u274c] [2026-01-23 05:13:44 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] CRITICAL VULNERABILITY: read_file.py does NOT use security/sandbox.py! The robust PathSandbox (symlink blocking, null byte checking) is NOT applied to read_file operations. Instead, read_file uses its own weaker _enforce_path_policy() which: (1) Does NOT block symlinks - uses .resolve() which follows them, (2) Does NOT check for null bytes, (3) Does NOT check URL-encoded traversal patterns. This is a significant security gap. | affected_tool=read_file; area=path_traversal; confidence=0.95; reasoning={\"how\": \"Searched for sandbox imports in read_file.py - no matches. Compared _enforce_path_policy logic vs PathSandbox.is_allowed logic.\", \"what\": \"Two separate path validation systems exist - one robust (sandbox.py) and one weak (_enforce_path_policy). The weak one is used for the most security-critical operation (file reading).\", \"why\": \"Grep confirmed read_file.py has no imports from security/sandbox module - the protections are not applied\"}; recommendation=Integrate security/sandbox.py into read_file.py path validation; severity=CRITICAL; stage=research; task=security_audit; vulnerability_type=security_bypass; priority=high; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:13:44.470991+00:00_63b5fa9f", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:13:44.471036+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-23T05:13:44.470991+00:00_63b5fa9f", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:13:44.482438+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 05:13:45 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-CodeAudit] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Import analysis reveals common pattern - all tools import server module creating potential circular dependency | confidence=0.85; imports={\"LoggingToolMixin\": 9, \"app\": 15, \"server_module\": 15}; issue=circular_import_risk; reasoning={\"how\": \"Analyzed import frequency across all tool files - server module is heavily imported by tools, creating bidirectional dependency\", \"what\": \"15 tools import 'from scribe_mcp.server import app' and 15 import 'from scribe_mcp import server as server_module'\", \"why\": \"Tools importing server creates tight coupling and potential circular dependencies since server imports tools/__init__.py\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:13:45.622951+00:00_9075d509", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:13:45.622990+00:00"}
