{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-23 05:13:48 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Performance] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Performance audit complete. Key findings: 1) No connection pooling - new SQLite connection per query. 2) State.json dual-write on every tool call. 3) Expensive startup: backend init, legacy migration, journal replay for up to 1000 projects, glob scanning. 4) Vector config loaded eagerly in settings. 5) query_entries does post-query filtering for message matching (inefficient). 6) Large validation functions (246 lines) on hot path. Ready to generate comprehensive research document. | audit_complete=True; confidence=0.9; findings_count=6; reasoning={\"how\": \"Systematic code inspection of startup sequence, storage layer, state management, and query implementations\", \"what\": \"Identified 6 major performance issues: connection pooling, dual writes, startup costs, eager loading, query inefficiency, validation overhead\", \"why\": \"Complete performance bottleneck analysis to guide optimization work\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:13:48.250719+00:00_1892a983", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:13:48.250768+00:00"}
