{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 05:14:15 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Dependency Analysis - requirements.txt: Dependencies use minimum version constraints (>=). Key dependencies: jinja2>=3.1.0 (template engine - potential SSTI if user input in templates), asyncpg>=0.29 (PostgreSQL), faiss-cpu/sentence-transformers (vector search). No pinned versions which could lead to supply chain issues. Jinja2 3.1.0 has autoescape enabled by default but should verify template usage. | area=dependencies; confidence=0.8; files_examined=[\"requirements.txt\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Read requirements.txt, analyzed version constraints and known vulnerability patterns for each library\", \"what\": \"Found 16 dependencies with minimum version constraints. Notable: jinja2 (SSTI risk), asyncpg (DB driver), faiss-cpu (native code)\", \"why\": \"Dependency versions can introduce known vulnerabilities - need to check for CVEs\"}; stage=research; task=security_audit; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:14:15.850844+00:00_3b4c392c", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:14:15.850888+00:00"}
