{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 05:14:27 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-CodeAudit] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Storage layer analysis - sqlite.py is 2666 lines, another massive file needing modular decomposition | confidence=1; file=storage/sqlite.py; issue_type=god_module; lines=2666; reasoning={\"how\": \"Checked file sizes - this follows the pattern of massive monolithic files seen elsewhere in codebase\", \"what\": \"SQLite storage backend contains all database logic in single 2666-line file - schema migrations, CRUD operations, session management, project management, and complex queries all mixed together\", \"why\": \"Storage backend should be split into migration, query, session, and project management modules\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:14:27.489496+00:00_9eac9061", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:14:27.489529+00:00"}
