{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 05:14:46 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Template Engine Security Analysis: MIXED FINDINGS. (1) GOOD: Supports SandboxedEnvironment and ImmutableSandboxedEnvironment modes, include_file() has path traversal protection (lines 282-284). (2) CONCERN: autoescape=False by default (line 224) - XSS risk if templates render user input as HTML. (3) CONCERN: Default security_mode may be 'none'/unrestricted based on normalization (lines 232-234). Need to verify default initialization. | area=template_injection; confidence=0.85; files_examined=[\"template_engine/engine.py\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Traced Jinja2 environment creation, examined security_mode handling, verified include_file path checks\", \"what\": \"Found sandbox modes available but autoescape disabled. include_file has proper path validation. Default mode unclear - could be unrestricted.\", \"why\": \"Jinja2 templates can be exploited for SSTI if user input reaches template rendering\"}; severity=MEDIUM; stage=research; task=security_audit; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:14:46.061003+00:00_df1fd574", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:14:46.061047+00:00"}
