{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 05:15:30 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Security] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Session/Agent Isolation Analysis: Database schema has proper session tables with foreign keys (agent_sessions, agent_projects, agent_project_events). Sessions tracked with session_id, agent_id, timestamps. Session heartbeat and end mechanisms exist. No obvious cross-session data leakage vectors found in schema. However, agent_id is user-provided without cryptographic verification - agents self-identify. This is acceptable for the intended use case (AI agents identifying themselves). | area=session_handling; confidence=0.85; files_examined=[\"storage/sqlite.py\", \"db/ops.py\", \"tools/agent_project_utils.py\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Examined database schema, session management functions, and agent identity handling\", \"what\": \"Found proper session tables with timestamps and foreign keys. agent_id is self-declared which is expected for AI agent use case. No cryptographic session verification but acceptable for threat model.\", \"why\": \"Session isolation is critical to prevent data leakage between different agent sessions\"}; severity=LOW; stage=research; task=security_audit; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:15:30.346132+00:00_292d9bf0", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:15:30.346183+00:00"}
