{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 05:24:42 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Imports] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Analyzed storage imports: storage/__init__.py imports BOTH SQLiteStorage AND PostgresStorage at module level. This is 2,666 lines of SQLite code + Postgres code loaded even though only one backend is ever used. Major lazy-load candidate. | confidence=0.95; finding=unnecessary_storage_imports; impact=Both storage backends imported at module load time, only one used; optimization=Lazy import unused storage backend based on settings.database_backend; reasoning={\"how\": \"Code inspection of storage/__init__.py dependencies - both backends imported regardless of settings.database_backend value\", \"what\": \"storage/__init__.py lines 9-10 import both PostgresStorage and SQLiteStorage unconditionally\", \"why\": \"Loading both storage backends wastes import time and memory when only one is ever used per process\"}; sqlite_size=2666 lines, 112KB; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:24:42.338482+00:00_fda28e37", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:24:42.338525+00:00"}
