{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 05:26:30 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Imports] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Found circular import risk: manage_docs imports append_entry (line 24), append_entry imports server module (line 16, 19). Both tools import from server.py which imports tools package. This creates server -> tools -> manage_docs -> append_entry -> server circular dependency. | confidence=0.9; cycle=[\"server.py\", \"tools/__init__.py\", \"manage_docs.py\", \"append_entry.py\", \"server.py\"]; finding=circular_import_pattern; reasoning={\"how\": \"Traced import chain from server.py line 660 -> tools/__init__.py -> manage_docs.py line 24 -> append_entry.py lines 16,19 -> back to server\", \"what\": \"Circular dependency: server imports tools, manage_docs imports append_entry, append_entry imports server\", \"why\": \"Circular imports are maintenance hazards and can cause import failures if order changes\"}; risk=Fragile import order dependency, could break with refactoring; workaround=Import at module level seems to work due to Python's import caching; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:26:30.289093+00:00_d4337697", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:26:30.289135+00:00"}
