{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 05:26:34 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Duplication] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] CRITICAL FINDING: 9 tools define nearly-identical Helper classes, all inheriting from LoggingToolMixin with same __init__ pattern (self.server_module = server_module). This is massive structural duplication - minimal helper classes that mostly exist to inherit LoggingToolMixin methods. The helpers add little functionality beyond what the mixin provides. | confidence=1; duplication_category=helper_classes; helper_count=9; pattern=class _XHelper(LoggingToolMixin): __init__ sets server_module; reasoning={\"how\": \"Located all Helper class definitions and instantiations, examined actual implementation to find they're mostly boilerplate\", \"what\": \"Found 9 Helper classes: _ReadRecentHelper, _QueryEntriesHelper, _ManageDocsHelper, _SetProjectHelper, _ListProjectsHelper, _GetProjectHelper, _HealthCheckHelper, _RotateLogHelper, _GenerateDocTemplatesHelper. All follow identical pattern: inherit LoggingToolMixin, set self.server_module. Most are near-empty boilerplate\", \"why\": \"This is the most significant duplication pattern discovered - indicates architectural smell\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:26:34.749003+00:00_91cd65da", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:26:34.749044+00:00"}
