{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-23 05:30:35 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Duplication] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] TOOL DUPLICATION ANALYSIS COMPLETE. Research phase finished successfully. Key findings: 1) 9 near-identical Helper classes (45-90 lines pure boilerplate), 2) 426 lines of parameter healing logic across 4 tools with manage_docs implementing custom healing despite shared utilities existing, 3) 50-100 lines of duplicated format routing, 4) 200-300 lines of inconsistent error handling. Total: 721-916 lines (6.7-8.6% of codebase). Critical insight: Shared utilities EXIST (BulletproofParameterCorrector, ErrorHandler, ResponseFormatter) but are inconsistently applied - this is INCOMPLETE REFACTORING not missing infrastructure. Refactoring roadmap prioritized with Quick Wins (helper consolidation, format routing) followed by Core Refactoring (healing framework, error handling). Estimated reduction: 350-500 lines (49-55%). Document ready for Architect stage. | confidence=0.9; investigation_time=~7 minutes; output_files=[\"RESEARCH_TOOL_DUPLICATION.md\"]; ready_for=Architect; reasoning={\"how\": \"Systematic code investigation using scribe.read_file (structure extraction, search, line-range inspection), grep pattern counting, cross-tool comparison, quantitative analysis. All findings verified with file:line references\", \"what\": \"Delivered complete duplication analysis: quantified duplication across 4 categories, identified root causes (incomplete refactoring), proposed 5 shared abstractions with priority ranking, estimated code reduction with confidence intervals, provided detailed handoff guidance\", \"why\": \"Research phase complete - all investigation objectives met with comprehensive findings and actionable recommendations\"}; research_complete=True; total_log_entries=10; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_