{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-23 05:33:14 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Database] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] SCHEMA INVENTORY COMPLETE: Identified 20 tables total. Core tables: scribe_projects, scribe_entries, scribe_metrics (3). Session management: agent_sessions, agent_projects, agent_project_events, scribe_sessions, session_projects, agent_recent_projects (6). Document management: doc_changes, dev_plans, phases, milestones, benchmarks, checklists, performance_metrics, document_sections, custom_templates, document_changes, sync_status, agent_report_cards, reminder_history (13). Found 21 explicit indexes created. Notable: Foreign key constraints present, ON DELETE CASCADE used extensively, CHECK constraints for enum-like fields. | agent=research; confidence=1; file_analyzed=storage/sqlite.py:820-1180; indexes_found=21; reasoning={\"how\": \"Systematic read_file line_range inspection of _initialise() method CREATE TABLE statements. Verified table structure, constraints, and existing indexes.\", \"what\": \"20 tables documented with columns, types, constraints, foreign keys. 3 core tables, 6 session tables, 13 document/metadata tables. All using TEXT for timestamps (SQLite convention), INTEGER primary keys, ON DELETE CASCADE for referential integrity.\", \"why\": \"Complete schema inventory is foundation for index analysis and query optimization recommendations\"}; stage=research; tables_found=20; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:33:14.467380+00:00_ed1d89d8", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:33:14.467422+00:00"}
