{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-23 05:33:44 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Formatter] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Master dispatcher analysis complete. finalize_tool_response (lines 2678-2945, 267 lines) is the central routing hub. It performs 3 responsibilities: 1) Logging to JSONL/SQL (lines 2678-2820, 142 lines), 2) Format routing based on tool_name (lines 2820-2945, 125 lines), 3) CallToolResult wrapping for MCP. Routes to 5 domain-specific formatters: format_readable_file_content (read_file), format_readable_log_entries (read_recent/query_entries), format_readable_append_entry (append_entry), format_readable_error (errors), plus generic JSON fallback. | confidence=1; logging_lines=142; method_size_lines=267; reasoning={\"how\": \"Line-by-line inspection using scribe.read_file to trace execution flow, counted responsibilities and line allocations\", \"what\": \"finalize_tool_response is NOT a formatter - it's a dispatcher + logger. Contains 3 distinct concerns: audit logging (142 lines extracting session context), format routing (125 lines with 5 tool-specific branches), MCP type wrapping. Constraint: ALL tools call this method, so decomposition must preserve the interface while splitting internal logic\", \"why\": \"Identify the central orchestration logic to understand decomposition boundaries\"}; routing_lines=125; routing_targets=5; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:33:44.091289+00:00_335fc597", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:33:44.091328+00:00"}
