{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 05:34:50 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Database] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] INDEX ANALYSIS COMPLETE for scribe_entries: Found 5 indexes: (1) idx_entries_project_ts (project_id, ts_iso DESC) - main composite, (2) idx_entries_priority_ts (priority, ts_iso DESC), (3) idx_entries_category_ts (category, ts_iso DESC), (4) idx_entries_project_priority_category (project_id, priority, category, ts_iso DESC) - mega composite, (5) idx_entries_log_type (project_id, log_type, ts_iso DESC). GAPS IDENTIFIED: (1) No index on 'agent' column - query_entries filters by agent IN (...) but must do full table scan, (2) No index on 'emoji' column - query_entries filters by emoji IN (...) but no index support, (3) json_extract(meta, '$.key') queries have NO index support (SQLite doesn't support functional indexes in this version). | agent=research; confidence=0.95; missing_indexes=[\"agent\", \"emoji\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Analyzed query_entries WHERE clause construction, cross-referenced with existing index definitions from lines 1066, 1305-1308. Identified filter columns without supporting indexes.\", \"what\": \"query_entries method (line 617-625) filters by agent and emoji but these columns have no indexes. Composite index (project_id, ts_iso DESC) exists but cannot be used when filtering by agent/emoji alone. json_extract queries also unindexed but require SQLite 3.9+ generated columns for indexing.\", \"why\": \"Missing indexes on frequently filtered columns cause full table scans, degrading query performance as data grows\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:34:50.404587+00:00_c47712fd", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:34:50.404667+00:00"}
