{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-23 05:35:36 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Formatter] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Method dependency mapping complete. Identified 3 dependency tiers: TIER 1 - Leaf utilities (no dependencies): _add_line_numbers, _parse_reasoning_block, _format_relative_time, _get_doc_line_count, _extract_compact_log_line, _truncate_message_smart. TIER 2 - UI builders (call Tier 1): _create_header_box, _create_footer_box, _format_table. TIER 3 - Domain formatters (call Tier 1+2): format_readable_file_content, format_readable_log_entries, format_readable_append_entry, format_readable_error, format_readable_confirmation, all project formatters. TIER 4 - Dispatcher (calls Tier 3): finalize_tool_response. This is a clean dependency hierarchy - extraction can proceed bottom-up. | confidence=0.95; dependency_tiers=4; has_circular_deps=False; reasoning={\"how\": \"Grep'd for self.method_name() patterns to find all internal method calls, traced call chains to identify dependency levels\", \"what\": \"Discovered clean 4-tier hierarchy with no circular dependencies. Tier 1 utilities are pure functions (stateless helpers). Tier 2 UI builders use Tier 1. Tier 3 domain formatters compose Tier 1+2. Tier 4 dispatcher routes to Tier 3. Constraint: can extract bottom-up (Tier 1 first) without breaking dependencies if we maintain imports\", \"why\": \"Map method call graph to determine safe extraction order\"}; tier1_count=6; tier2_count=3; tier3_count=10; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:35:36.735089+00:00_1f19f813", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:35:36.735260+00:00"}
