{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 05:36:12 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Database] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] DATA VOLUME ANALYSIS COMPLETE: Found 3 auto-cleanup mechanisms: (1) doc_changes table: Hard limit of 500 entries per project, auto-deletes oldest when exceeded (lines 436-445), (2) agent_sessions: Expires-based cleanup, batch deletion of expired sessions (lines 2178-2187), (3) reminder_history: Time-based cleanup, deletes entries older than cutoff_hours (lines 2314-2323). CONCERN: scribe_entries has NO cleanup mechanism - grows unbounded! This is the main data volume table and will become massive over time. No archival, no rotation at DB level (only JSONL rotation exists at file level). | agent=research; cleanup_exists=[\"doc_changes\", \"agent_sessions\", \"reminder_history\"]; confidence=1; reasoning={\"how\": \"Searched for DELETE operations, analyzed cleanup logic, verified scribe_entries has no retention policy. Cross-referenced with rotate_log tool (file rotation only, not DB).\", \"what\": \"scribe_entries is main log table storing ALL project entries with no cleanup. Only file-level rotation exists (rotate_log tool) but DB entries remain. Other tables: scribe_projects/metrics also unbounded but grow slowly. doc_changes has 500-entry limit, agent_sessions expire, reminder_history has time-based cleanup.\", \"why\": \"Unbounded table growth causes database bloat, slow queries, and eventual performance degradation\"}; stage=research; unbounded_tables=[\"scribe_entries\", \"scribe_projects\", \"scribe_metrics\"]; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T05:36:12.804609+00:00_d2b26ecc", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T05:36:12.804679+00:00"}
