{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 07:01:57 UTC] [Agent: ArchitectAgent-Phase5Update] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Architecture decision: Adopting research-recommended 6-phase extraction order (UI->Base->File->Entry->Project->Dispatcher) over original 4-task plan (Base->UI->Domain->Dispatcher). Rationale: (1) UI helpers are lowest risk with good test coverage - safe first extraction, (2) Base infrastructure needed by all others - extract early, (3) File formatter is HIGH VALUE at 605 lines but needs tests first, (4) Entry/Project are medium risk with moderate dependencies, (5) Dispatcher is HIGHEST RISK - async router with MCP SDK dependency - must be last. | alternatives_rejected=[\"original_order_base_first\", \"alphabetical\", \"size_ordered\"]; chosen=risk_ordered_ui_first; decision=extraction_order; reasoning={\"how\": \"Analyzed test coverage gaps and dependency graph from research - acyclic dependencies allow any order but risk-ordering provides safest path\", \"what\": \"Research found UI helpers have 8+ tests each, dispatcher has async MCP dependency and no dedicated tests, format_readable_file_content has 0 direct tests despite being 605 lines\", \"why\": \"Risk-ordered extraction minimizes chance of breaking production while allowing early wins with well-tested UI helpers\"}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T07:01:57.214232+00:00_12ea5048", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T07:01:57.214273+00:00"}
