{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-23 07:58:16 UTC] [Agent: CoderAgent-Phase5-ProjectFormatter] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Fixed f-string syntax error in ProjectFormatter. Python f-strings cannot have backslash escapes inside expression parts (e.g., `{'\\u2550' * 58}`). Solution: Added class constants for all Unicode box-drawing characters (BOX_TOP_LEFT, BOX_TOP_RIGHT, BOX_BOTTOM_LEFT, BOX_BOTTOM_RIGHT, BOX_HORIZONTAL, BOX_VERTICAL) and emojis (EMOJI_CLIPBOARD, EMOJI_FOLDER, EMOJI_CHART, EMOJI_PAGE, EMOJI_BULB, EMOJI_SEARCH, EMOJI_TARGET, EMOJI_OPEN_FOLDER, EMOJI_PUSHPIN, EMOJI_LABEL, STAR, BULLET, CHECK). Updated all problematic f-strings in format_project_detail, format_no_projects_found, format_project_context, format_project_sitrep_new, and format_project_sitrep_existing to use these constants instead of inline escape sequences. | files=[\"utils/formatters/project.py\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Added 19 class constants for Unicode characters, refactored 12 f-string expressions across 5 methods\", \"what\": \"Python f-string limitation with backslash escapes, resolved by extracting constants\", \"why\": \"Fix syntax error preventing import of ProjectFormatter\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T07:58:16.061898+00:00_34be2762", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T07:58:16.061957+00:00"}
