{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 09:14:51 UTC] [Agent: CoderAgent-TestFix-SetProject] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] Root cause found: detect_project_state uses docs_were_generated flag to distinguish NEW vs EXISTING. When docs are generated (truly new project), state=NEW. When docs already exist (including from a previous test run in the SAME tmpdir), state=EXISTING_LEGACY. The test is seeing EXISTING because the temp directory has leftover project state from test setup. The test expectations are actually CORRECT - the bug is that we're not cleaning up database state between tests. | fix_needed=tests need to ensure clean database state OR use truly unique project paths; reasoning={\"how\": \"Either clean database between tests or use unique project IDs that include test isolation\", \"what\": \"Tests reuse same database, previous test runs leave project records\", \"why\": \"detect_project_state correctly identifies projects with existing docs as EXISTING\"}; root_cause=database_state_not_cleaned_between_tests; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T09:14:51.491385+00:00_0867965c", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T09:14:51.491429+00:00"}
