{"op": "append", "content": "[\u274c] [2026-01-23 09:17:01 UTC] [Agent: CoderAgent-TestFix-SetProject] [Project: scribe_codebase_audit] BUG FOUND! Line 573 of set_project.py checks doc_result.get('files', []) but _ensure_documents returns 'generated' key (line 799), NOT 'files'. This causes docs_were_generated to always be False when docs already exist, triggering EXISTING_LEGACY state even for truly new projects. The key mismatch is the root cause. | bug_location=set_project.py line 573; fix=Change line 573 to check 'generated' key instead of 'files'; impact=NEW projects incorrectly show as EXISTING when docs exist; issue=key mismatch: checks 'files' but function returns 'generated'; reasoning={\"how\": \"Change to doc_result.get('generated', []) to match actual return value\", \"what\": \"doc_result.get('files', []) always returns empty list causing docs_were_generated=False\", \"why\": \"Line 573 comment says 'returns files key' but _ensure_documents actually returns 'generated' key\"}; priority=high; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_codebase_audit/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T09:17:01.931395+00:00_909d5787", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T09:17:01.931484+00:00"}
